    "description_stripped": "This is the methodology and reproducibility sidecar for the AI-run mathematical translation program. It preserves interlanguage source baselines, weighted-automaton and terminology work, manager handoffs, Interslavic normalization evidence, Romance-language infrastructure, reusable scripts, and bounded translation experiments.\nOpen first: 00_Interlanguage_Methodology_Current_v11_20260718.pdf. It maps the current record and explains the new Noether R823 completion gate without presenting infrastructure as a finished language edition.\nNew in v0.11: 15_Noether_R823_Translation_Completion_Gate_v4_20260718.zip contains the exact 35-check gate, adversarial replay, readable final audit, structured all-page visual-review record, terminology locator audit, and a complete 473-page candidate-derived render baseline under a pinned 120-dpi Poppler profile. The Spanish replay passes all 35 declared checks against the verified R823 authority and exact current 473-page candidate. All 81 declared units are source-reconciled in the evidence graph; 68 independently hash-pinned native Spanish TeX line witnesses meet the terminology-source minimum, while 33 target-only decisions remain visible but excluded.\nRomance v10: the record continues to carry the current Romance routing, source, WordWeb, semantic-alignment, access, bounded-production, and QA infrastructure. It records 61 language or variety routes, 60 concepts, 106 senses, 682 reviewed occurrence records, and six bounded controlled-Romance tranches. It contains zero human intelligibility observations and does not claim a completed Romance translation or empirical intelligibility result.\nClassification: the passing Spanish gate certifies the declared scope, artifact, evidence, build, and render bindings. It is not native-language certification, peer review, proof of semantic perfection, mathematical proof checking, or critical-edition certification. The French R823 lane remains active and moving. The actual Spanish reader and editable translation package are published on 10.5281/zenodo.21422620 under the Noether concept DOI.\nGitHub: corrections and improved evidence can be proposed through issues or pull requests at https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts.",
